   <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6718">
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">propagation process</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Process by which a disturbance at one point is propagated to another point more remote from the source with no net transport of the material of the medium itself; examples include the motion of electromagnetic waves, sound waves, hydrodynamic waves in liquids, and vibration waves in solids.</skos:scopeNote>
